A||||10||Tom88gt||which low temp fan switch and thermostat?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||04-30-2001||08:40 PM||||Any opinions on which low tempature fan switch and thermostat to use.  There are several different ones to choose from and thus multiple combinations.  Fiero Store and Rodney sell different items so there are three different items (including the stock ones).<P>Thermostats - 160'/180'/195'<BR>Switches - 176'/200'/225'<P>My 88 V-6 is stock and will remain so until it blows up.  No ECM chip or anything.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||04-30-2001||09:40 PM||||I believe that the 160 'stat need a different  ECM chip the others are fine, also don't get a fan switch that's lower than your 'stat(the fan would never shut off). My choice would be the 180 stat and 200 switch( not based on anything)||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-30-2001||09:52 PM||||Ive got V6 with turbo. I use a Hypertech 160* thermo and 175*  FAN SWITCH. been in it now for 3 years. only goes up 1/3 way even on 95* day with AC on.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||04-30-2001||10:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Ive got V6 with turbo. I use a Hypertech 160* thermo and 175* FAN SWITCH. been in it now for 3 years. only goes up 1/3 way even on 95* day with AC on.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So did you get those because of the turbo? Or is this a smart move with just the stock 2.8?? Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-01-2001||07:57 AM||||yes. with stock 195* car wouldnt hardly run, spit, sputtered, cutout, you name it. 180* helped, but still coughed a little at higher rpms. 160* totally eliminiated the prob. runs smooth now till 7000-7500 rpm, where my rev limiter is set.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wade87GT||05-01-2001||09:57 AM||||I've got a stock V6 and chip with the Hypertech 160* thermostat and 175* Fan Switch, both from the Fiero Store. I've had this setup for about three years also. The car never runs hot and everthing works the way it should. It feels like it has much more power and torque, over stock, in the low to middle range. It does start to run out of steam over 6000 RPM. Expect to use more gas since it's running cooler, thus richer.<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000006||Formula88||05-01-2001||01:40 PM||||Anyone running the Hypertech Thermomaster chip with the 160* thermo and fan switch?  Can you tell a difference?  Note: I'm not talking about the street runner chip, only the Thermomaster.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tom88gt||05-01-2001||09:07 PM||||Wade87GT...do you mean that you are using the stock factory ecm chip or that you have a stock engine with aftermarket chip, stat and switch?<P>What mileage are you getting?  City/Hwy?||||reg||5
Z||000008||Thecrewchief1||05-01-2001||11:59 PM||||I also run the 160 stat with the 176 switch, so far it works great. Bill||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wade87GT||05-02-2001||12:46 PM||||Tom88gt, I have a stock engine and stock chip. I did recently install a Borla exhaust with a "test pipe", which works really well. I haven't checked my mpg in years, but I'll do it soon and let you know.<P>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tom88gt||05-02-2001||09:28 PM||||I'm getting low to mid 20s MPG daily driving.  And that is peppy driving too.<P>On the highway I get upper 20s to almost 30 MPG while doing 75-80 MPH. <P>My engine is stock with 115,000 miles.  Not even a K&N or anything.  So I'm a little hesitant to mess with a good thing.||||reg||7
